#!/usr/bin/env bash
# kaomoji: searchable kaomoji picker for Wayland (KDE Plasma, Sway, Hyprland...)
# https://github.com/solotilimeow/kaomoji-picker
#
# Needs fuzzel 1.11 or newer and wl-clipboard; libnotify (notify-send) is
# optional and shows a "Copied" notification. On Arch:
#   sudo pacman -S --needed fuzzel wl-clipboard libnotify
#
# Press your shortcut, type a word ("shrug", "cat", "flip table"...),
# pick one with Enter, then paste it with Ctrl+V.
#
# Built in: 3179 kaomoji (the list at the bottom of this file).
# Your own: ~/.config/kaomoji.txt, one per line: the kaomoji, then
# 3 spaces, then search words. Yours are listed first, and updating
# this script never touches that file. Duplicates are hidden.
#
# Most built-in entries come from kaomoji-collection
# (https://github.com/kaomojiya-collection/kaomoji-collection). The block
# marked "from rofimoji" near the end comes from rofimoji
